  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SALAR Inclusive Local Governance MENA 2023-2025 - NEW SKR MENA 2023 - 2025</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">SKR inkluderande lokal demokrati  MENA 2023-2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Det &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;let f&#xf6;r programmet &#xe4;r att st&#xf6;dja kapacitetsutveckling av  strategiska f&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndringsakt&#xf6;rer som kan bidra till f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrat lokalt genomf&#xf6;rande samt policydialog vad g&#xe4;ller lokal demokrati i MENA-regionen.  Programmet som genomf&#xf6;rs  av Sveriges f&#xf6;rbund f&#xf6;r  kommuner och regioner (SKR) och deras eget bolag SALAR International avser engagera ett 50-tal deltagare fr&#xe5;n fem l&#xe4;nder i regionen under en 24-m&#xe5;naders period.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the programme is to support the capacity development of a critical mass of strategic change agents who can contribute to improved local practices, as well as policy dialogue, on decentralisation and local governance in the MENA region. The programme managed by the Swedish association for local authorities and regions, will engage around 50 participants from five countries in the region for a period of 24 months.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The programme focuses on strengthening the achievement of regional and national priorities enhancing local governance and local development in the MENA-region and to contribute to establishing an enabling environment for decentralisation policy reform.

The overall objective of the programme is to support the capacity development of a critical mass of strategic change agents who can contribute to improved local practices and policy dialogue on decentralisation and local governance in the MENA region.

The programme will engage around 50 strategically selected individuals from  five targeted countries, expanding knowledge and enhancing capacities among key national and local stakeholders to drive local governance and development change during challenging circumstances and to foster a sustained regional community of practice and decentralisation advocacy. 

To achieve these outcomes, the program will support the capacity development to foster actor driven change through a regional platform for those having the tools, skills and commitment working towards decentralisation. Beyond, it will help establish effective collaborative links between civil society, local elected officials and technical services to ensure their participation in decision-making. As it will be better informed, civil society will be well prepared to negotiate the inclusion of its needs in development processes and exercise control over access to basic social services. The capacity development programme aims to contribute on two levels long term:

Organisational level: i) Increased motivation and capacity for application of different instruments for more accountable local governance, participatory planning, fact- and evidence based decision-making, and improved local development.

Individual level: i) Enhanced knowledge, skills and commitment to decentralisation, local governance and local development and services, and in areas such as gender equality, climate change and environment, and migration; ii) Strengthening of peer to peer collaborative learning skills, networking, change management and policy advocacy.</narrative>
  </description>
